Q: How to setup PhpStorm / WebStorm to work with Vite aliases? A: <p>In case this helps someone, I automated entio's answer by adding a vite plugin like this.</p>
<p>Where my aliases are defined like this and passed to Vite:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const alias = {
  '@': path.join(__dirname, './src/renderer/src'),
  static: path.resolve(__dirname, '../static'),
  Core: path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/core'),
  Main: path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/main'),  
  Custom: path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/custom/'),
  Store: path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/renderer/src/store/'),
  Views: path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/renderer/src/components/views'), 
  Router: path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/renderer/src/router'),
  NM: path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules'),
  Root: path.resolve(__dirname, '.'),
  crypto: 'crypto-browserify',
  stream: 'stream-browserify',
  zlib: 'browserify-zlib',
  buffer: 'buffer/',
  util: 'util/'
}
</code></pre>
<p>And this is provided to the plugins array</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>{
  name: 'phpstorm-config-generator',
  configureServer() {
    const fs = require('fs')
    const path = require('path')
    const aliasObj = alias
    const paths = {}
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(aliasObj)) {
      if (typeof value === 'string') {
        const aliasKey = key.endsWith('/*') ? key : key + '/*'
        const aliasValue = value.endsWith('/*') ? value : value + '/*'
        paths[aliasKey] = aliasValue
      }
    }
    const configContent =
      'System.config({\n  &quot;paths&quot;: ' + JSON.stringify(paths, null, 4) + '\n});\n'
    fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(__dirname, 'phpstorm.config.js'), configContent, 'utf8')
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The result is created each time you run dev or build.  You might need to add it to your ignore list for your linter and formatter since the file doesn't look perfect and would keep getting refreshed every time you ran dev.</p>

Q: Button hover state gets stuck on touch devices after tap (works fine for mouse) A: <p>This behavior happens because <strong>touch devices don’t really have hover</strong>, but browsers still <strong>simulate <code>:hover</code> on tap</strong>.<br />
So when you tap a button on mobile, the <code>:hover</code> styles get applied and stay there until something else is touched.</p>
<p>The correct way to handle this is <strong>not JavaScript</strong>.<br />
The fix is to <strong>limit hover styles only to devices that actually support a mouse pointer</strong>.</p>
<h3><strong>The key fix (media query)</strong></h3>
<pre><code>@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  .btn:hover {
    background: #2fb7d9;
    color: #000;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>This media query means:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><code>hover: hover</code> → the device truly supports hover</p>
</li>
<li><p><code>pointer: fine</code> → the device uses a precise pointer (mouse / trackpad)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Touch screens use <code>pointer: coarse</code>, so they <strong>never enter this block</strong>, which completely prevents the “stuck hover” issue.</p>
<h3><strong>Example:</strong></h3>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.btn {
  background: #000;
  color: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #2fb7d9;
  padding: 12px 28px;
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: 16px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease, transform 0.12s ease;
  -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
}

/* Hover ONLY for real pointer devices */
@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  .btn:hover {
    background: #2fb7d9;
    color: #000;
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button class="btn"&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: react-map-gl Marker is moving when zooming the map A: <p>hello its maybe too late but for next, just ensure you have your projection set. If you let projection undefined I think it recompute it on zoom / moving on map</p>
<pre><code>import MapboxMap, { MapRef, Marker, Popup } from &quot;react-map-gl&quot;;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>&lt;MapboxMap
  ref={mapRef}
